# Git Conventions

## Branch Naming

```
feature/description     # Nova feature
bugfix/description      # Correcao de bug
hotfix/description      # Fix urgente em producao
refactor/description    # Refatoracao
test/description        # Adicao de testes
docs/description        # Documentacao
```

### Exemplos
```
feature/cognito-password-reset
bugfix/null-pointer-user-service
refactor/extract-validation-logic
test/add-cognito-service-tests
```

## Commit Messages

### Formato
```
<type>: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer]
```

### Types
| Type | Descricao |
|------|-----------|
| `feat` | Nova feature |
| `fix` | Correcao de bug |
| `test` | Adicao/correcao de testes |
| `docs` | Documentacao |
| `refactor` | Refatoracao (sem mudar comportamento) |
| `style` | Formatacao (sem mudar logica) |
| `perf` | Melhoria de performance |
| `chore` | Manutencao (deps, configs) |
| `ci` | CI/CD changes |

### Exemplos
```bash
feat: Add user password reset functionality

fix: Resolve null pointer exception in UserService

test: Add unit tests for CognitoService

docs: Update API documentation for auth endpoints

refactor: Extract validation logic to separate class

chore: Update Spring Boot to 4.0.0
```

## Workflow

### 1. Criar Branch
```bash
git checkout -b feature/new-feature
```

### 2. Desenvolver (TDD!)
- Escrever testes primeiro
- Implementar feature
- Garantir que testes passam

### 3. Commit
```bash
git add .
git commit -m "feat: implement user registration"
```

### 4. Push
```bash
git push origin feature/new-feature
```

### 5. Pull Request
- Descricao clara
- Referenciar issues relacionadas
- Solicitar code review

## Pre-Merge Checklist

- [ ] Todos os testes passam (`mvn test`)
- [ ] Coverage >= 80%
- [ ] Sem warnings de compilacao
- [ ] Codigo segue style guide
- [ ] Commit messages semanticos
- [ ] Documentacao atualizada
- [ ] Sem dados sensiveis no codigo
